ater the Fantastic Four began shrinking  randomly so with the help of Hank Pym  they shrink down to investigate  realizing that dr. doom didn't disappear  he just shrunk down into the Microverse  and he's been spending all this time  living in the star system of subatomic  a' conquering a world called mir wood so  during this time in a Microverse we also  meet the lizard men of the planet talk  or talk before the Fantastic Four gets  saved by ant-man and a Doctor Doom  please lead in the comics there's a  character cycle man from subatomic ax he  gets involved when the Silver Surfer  hides from Galactus in the Micra  and there's a later Marvel Microverse  story when Scott Lang shrinks down into  microworld to look for the thing and he  finds him living it up down there as a  gladiator fighter the storylines  actually very similar to thor ragnarok  within this whole Microverse there's  also a place called homeworld which is  kind of a molecular chain planet that  was conquered by this figure named Baron  kartha it's inhabitants possess a world  mind it's kind of a shared sentience  that can be controlled by one leader and  tapped as an energy source  so really the microworld just contains a  lot of different colorful characters and  races of civilizations and locations  that are just established in the Marvel  Comics that the MCU could draw upon to  adapt into the quantum realm in the  movies so this thing that we saw in  ant-man the wasp if it's a city perhaps  it could be an MCU version of mere wood  or Tok Tok or homeworld and maybe this  places inhabitants could be characters  like The Lizard Men or Baron cars Oh or  cycle band or something completely new  entirely really it's too soon to say  whether the quantum realm is how the MCU  plans to introduce a fantastic for  Doctor Doom Silver Surfer you know since  Disney will soon acquire Fox's Marvel  properties and yeah it's probably too  soon to determine if Janet Van Dyne is  lying about evolution could be a clue  pointing out the x-men which is another  Fox Marvel property that will eventually  join the Disney Marvel Studios family  but you know very watching ant-man the  wasp and hearing all this frequent  techno jargon about quantum physics and  quantum everything it suggests to me  that the future the MCU may go even  deeper into science and theoretical  physics one area study examines the  connection between inner space the space  between atoms and outer space the space  between stars and galaxies but there is  that assuming that the universe spawned  from the Big Bang the explosion of one  particle that the laws that govern  gravity and motion and the vast reaches  of the universe must be the same as the  laws on the tiniest scale within matter  my point is is that maybe we shouldn't  see the quantum realm as like a dead end  just some expanse where you can just get  lost in perhaps we should see it as a  kind of tunnel that leads to something  else  remember the quantum realm did show up  briefly as one of the many dimensions  Doctor Strange floated through so if  it's among the mystic powers of the  sorcerer supreme to traverse through  this place it could be more of a bridge  than a bottomless pit  so I think it's possible that Scott Lang  doesn't need to be rescued from the  quantum realm maybe he just needs to go  deeper into it to see what's on the  other side perhaps we'll find an  einstein-rosen bridge which is something  that we have seen before in the MCU  remember The Devil's anus I'm Thor  Ragnarok and every time the Bifrost has  been opened up it's a wormhole that  leads to some other realm and space so  if Scott emerges out of the other side  of a wormhole with some kind of quantum  healing energy that he's gathering in  that post-credits scene I could see that  being very useful for Tony Stark and the  rest of the surviving Avengers in their  final fight with Thanos there's also the  theory that the quantum realm could  cause a phase shift into a paral